From: hashtagbasit <53941105+hashtagbasit@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] scsi: ufs: core: power the device down before removing the host

ufshcd_remove() cut VCC and the clocks with the device still active and the
link up. Unbinding the controller in a loop reset the whole board within
1 to 50 cycles (measured on the Pocket FIT, SM8650, reset with no panic or
log). The same teardown runs on this SoC, where a sleep from an SD card
install unbinds the idle UFS host, so a sleep could reset the handheld.

Remove the logical units, which flushes their caches, then send the device
to POWERDOWN with the link off as the shutdown path does, and only then
remove the SCSI host. Clean over 60 cycles on each of 3 boots on the Pocket FIT
against resets at 1, 8 and 50 without it. A clock hold across the teardown did
not help.
---
diff --git a/drivers/ufs/core/ufshcd.c b/drivers/ufs/core/ufshcd.c
--- a/drivers/ufs/core/ufshcd.c
+++ b/drivers/ufs/core/ufshcd.c
@@ -10972,6 +10972,32 @@
 }
 
 /**
+ * ufshcd_power_down_device - power the device down before the host is removed
+ * @hba: per adapter instance
+ *
+ * Removing the host cuts the device supplies, so the device has to reach
+ * POWERDOWN with the link off first, as it does on shutdown. The logical units
+ * go first so their caches are flushed while the device still takes commands.
+ * The device WLUN stays, it carries the START STOP UNIT.
+ */
+static void ufshcd_power_down_device(struct ufs_hba *hba)
+{
+	struct scsi_device *sdev;
+
+	shost_for_each_device(sdev, hba->host) {
+		if (sdev != hba->ufs_device_wlun)
+			scsi_remove_device(sdev);
+	}
+
+	down(&hba->host_sem);
+	hba->shutting_down = true;
+	up(&hba->host_sem);
+
+	if (__ufshcd_wl_suspend(hba, UFS_SHUTDOWN_PM))
+		dev_warn(hba->dev, "device not powered down before removal\n");
+}
+
+/**
  * ufshcd_remove - de-allocate SCSI host and host memory space
  *		data structure memory
  * @hba: per adapter instance
@@ -10988,8 +11014,11 @@
 	blk_mq_destroy_queue(hba->tmf_queue);
 	blk_put_queue(hba->tmf_queue);
 	blk_mq_free_tag_set(&hba->tmf_tag_set);
-	if (hba->scsi_host_added)
+	if (hba->scsi_host_added) {
+		if (hba->ufs_device_wlun)
+			ufshcd_power_down_device(hba);
 		scsi_remove_host(hba->host);
+	}
 	/* disable interrupts */
 	ufshcd_disable_intr(hba, hba->intr_mask);
 	ufshcd_hba_stop(hba);
